# React architecture

React 18.2, Vite, React Router 6, TanStack Query 5, and Redux Toolkit. There is no React Server Components boundary.

Use function components. Keep a component to one job. Compose existing pieces in `client/src/components` before adding a new one.

Prefer derived values over state that copies props. Keep state in the component that owns the interaction. Do not add an effect to copy one state value into another.

Do not memoize unless a measured render problem says so. Do not add global state for data that belongs in a query or in one screen.

List rendering needs a stable id from the data, not the array index, when the list can reorder.

For performance detail, read `.agents/skills/vercel-react-best-practices/SKILL.md` and skip every Next.js-only rule. For component API shape, read `.agents/skills/vercel-composition-patterns/SKILL.md` and skip React 19 APIs (`use`, ref-as-prop) until this app upgrades.

Do not create a compound component when a single component with a few clear props is enough.
